    Bug 2036628 - Clear cached EWS outgoing password so compose bad-password tests start without credentials. r=edicharry



    This fixes an intermittent nsGlobalWindowInner leak observed on Mac debug.

    After bug 1985223 (D295506), EWS outgoing servers cache passwords via
    MsgPasswordAuthModule. Clearing the login manager is therefore no longer
    sufficient to reset all credential state.

    As a result, tests expecting no saved credentials could start with a
    cached in-memory password, preventing the password prompt from appearing
    and causing timeouts and subsequent shutdown leaks.

    Clear the cached EWS password in tests that expect no credentials so they
    start in a consistent state across platforms.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298331

